---
/**
 * Percentiles — why a performance report quotes p95 and not the average.
 *
 * A response-time distribution with a long right tail: the average sits in the
 * quiet part, and every complaint comes from the part it hides.
 */
---

<figure class="lu-figure percentiles">
  <div class="lu-figure__frame lu-figure__scroll">
    <svg viewBox="0 24 640 216" role="img" aria-label="A right-skewed response-time distribution. The average sits near the peak, while p95 and p99 sit far out in the tail where the slow requests are.">
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="pc-fill" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
          <stop offset="0%" stop-color="var(--sl-color-gray-4)" stop-opacity="0.22" />
          <stop offset="100%" stop-color="var(--sl-color-gray-4)" stop-opacity="0.02" />
        </linearGradient>
      </defs>

      <!-- distribution -->
      <path
        class="curve-fill"
        d="M60 190 C120 190 130 60 176 60 C214 60 226 138 266 156 C320 180 360 174 420 180 C480 186 540 188 596 189 L596 190 Z"
      />
      <path
        class="curve"
        d="M60 190 C120 190 130 60 176 60 C214 60 226 138 266 156 C320 180 360 174 420 180 C480 186 540 188 596 189"
      />

      <!-- baseline -->
      <line class="axis" x1="60" y1="190" x2="608" y2="190" />
      <text class="axis-label" x="60" y="206">faster</text>
      <text class="axis-label axis-label--end" x="608" y="206">slower</text>

      <!-- the average -->
      <line class="mark mark--mean" x1="196" y1="52" x2="196" y2="190" />
      <text class="mark-label mark-label--mean" x="196" y="42">average</text>
      <text class="mark-note" x="196" y="226">what a report usually quotes</text>

      <!-- percentiles -->
      <line class="mark" x1="404" y1="96" x2="404" y2="190" />
      <text class="mark-label" x="404" y="88">p95</text>
      <line class="mark" x1="536" y1="96" x2="536" y2="190" />
      <text class="mark-label" x="536" y="88">p99</text>

      <!-- the tail -->
      <path class="brace" d="M404 214 L404 220 L596 220 L596 214" />
      <text class="tail" x="500" y="236">every complaint you will receive</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="lu-figure__caption">
    Step 13. The average is not wrong, it is answering a question nobody asked.
    State which percentile the threshold uses, and gate on that.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .lu-figure__scroll svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 560px;
    height: auto;
  }

  .curve {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .curve-fill {
    fill: url(#pc-fill);
    stroke: none;
  }

  .axis {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .axis-label {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
  }

  .axis-label--end {
    text-anchor: end;
  }

  .mark {
    stroke: var(--lu-marker);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }

  .mark--mean {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
  }

  .mark-label {
    fill: var(--lu-marker);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }

  .mark-label--mean {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  .mark-note {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }

  .brace {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .tail {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
</style>
